 - **Measured Performance:** DVGO is significantly faster than NeRF in both training and inference due to the replacement of MLP queries with grid lookups [S1, unofficial]. It achieves 2-3x speedup with PyTorch CUDA extensions [S1, unofficial].
 - **Scaling:** Scales linearly with grid resolution. Higher resolutions require more memory but offer better detail. Octree or hash encoding variants can be used for scaling to higher resolutions [S1, unofficial].
-- **Strengths:** Fast training and inference, simple implementation, efficient memory usage for moderate resolutions.
-- **Limitations:** Memory usage grows cubically with resolution. May suffer from aliasing artifacts at high resolutions if not properly filtered. Less flexible than MLPs for complex geometries.
-- **When to Use:** When training speed is critical and the scene can be represented well with a voxel grid. Suitable for forward-facing and bounded scenes.
-- **When Not to Use:** For very large unbounded scenes where memory is a constraint, or when high-frequency details require very high grid resolutions.
